== Contact
Email: [amandlek@stanford.edu]

== Recent News

- \[July 2020\] We are organizing the [https://sites.google.com/utexas.edu/rss-2020-imitation-learning/home?authuser=0 Advances and Challenges in Imitation Learning for Robotics] workshop at [https://roboticsconference.org/ RSS 2020].

- \[July 2020\] Our new algorithm, Generalization Through Imitation (GTI), will appear at [https://roboticsconference.org/ RSS 2020]. It enables learning visuomotor control from human demonstrations and generalizing to new long-horizon tasks by leveraging latent compositional structures. See our [https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.06085 paper], [https://sites.google.com/view/gti2020/ website], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hlvRmLlYHZ0 video] for more details.

- \[May 2020\] Our [http://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05321 paper] on offline learning from large-scale robot manipulation datasets appeared at [http://icra2020.org/ ICRA 2020]. We demonstrated that our algorithm can learn from our [http://roboturk.stanford.edu/dataset.html crowdsourced RoboTurk dataset] without requiring additional interaction. See our [http://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05321 paper], [https://sites.google.com/stanford.edu/iris/ website], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7P41XHVHtM&feature=emb_title talk] for more details!

== About Me

I am a PhD candidate in the [http://svl.stanford.edu/ Stanford Vision and Learning Lab] advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. I work on applying Reinforcement Learning and Imitation Learning to Robotics. In particular, I'm interested in building systems and algorithms to allow robots to leverage human insight for manipulation. 

